# {{ project.name }} – Flutter

The UI is a Flutter app, the logic is the Rust library in the project folder
(flutter_rust_bridge). Freya TDE generates `lib/freya/*.g.dart` and the bridge
`lib/src/rust/`; `lib/main.dart` and `pubspec.yaml` are yours.

## Run

```sh
cargo build                     # in the project folder
cd flutter
flutter create --platforms={{ project.platforms | join(",") if project.platforms else "linux,windows,macos" }} .   # once
flutter run
```

`flutter create .` only adds the missing platform folders and leaves existing
files alone.

## Release

```sh
cd flutter
flutter build {{ (project.platforms | first) if project.platforms else "linux" }} --release
```

`rust_builder/` (cargokit) builds the Rust library with `cargo` and bundles it
into the program (Linux `bundle/lib/`, Windows next to the `.exe`, macOS into
the `.app`). Needs `rustup` (cargokit uses it to check the target).

## Window

Title, size, minimum/maximum size, position and start state are set by
`<Form>View.setupWindow()` (from the designer, via window_manager) at start.
